294 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 133 0 R
/E (SmartGreen monitors the available water supply and tracks how much water is used for plant irrigation. The application can also simulate rainwater collection and store the collected water in a virtual water reserve. This allows the system to demonstrate how water can be used more efficiently and helps reduce unnecessary consumption.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
295 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 133 0 R
/E (The application monitors energy consumption from different greenhouse systems, such as lighting, ventilation, and heating. By tracking energy usage, SmartGreen can show which systems consume the most resources and help the user understand how to manage the greenhouse more efficiently.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
296 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 133 0 R
/E (SmartGreen collects information about the greenhouse and displays it in the form of statistics and graphs. Users can monitor water consumption, energy usage, plant conditions, and harvest results over time. This information helps users better understand how the greenhouse is performing.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
297 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 133 0 R
/E (Resource Efficiency)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
298 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 133 0 R
/E (By combining water management, energy monitoring, and statistics, SmartGreen focuses not only on automation but also on efficient resource use. The system allows users to see how their decisions and automatic settings affect the overall performance of the greenhouse.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
