330 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 135 0 R
/E (The first stage of the project is research and planning. We will study how modern smart greenhouse systems work and identify the most important conditions that need to be monitored. Based on this research, we will define the main functions of SmartGreen and plan how different parts of the application will work together.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
331 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 135 0 R
/E (During this stage, we will design the visual appearance and structure of the application. We plan to create a clear and modern Dashboard, an interactive greenhouse visualization, plant monitoring pages, a greenhouse map, and notification screens. The goal is to make the application easy to understand while also making it visually interesting and interactive.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
332 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 135 0 R
/E (The next stage is the development of the main software functions. We will create a system that simulates greenhouse conditions such as temperature, soil moisture, air humidity, and lighting. We will also develop automation rules, manual controls, notifications, resource monitoring, and statistics.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
333 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 135 0 R
/E (The final stage is testing the application. We will check how the system responds when different greenhouse conditions change and whether the automatic functions work correctly. For example, we will test whether ventilation activates when the temperature becomes too high and whether automatic watering starts when soil moisture becomes too low. We will also test the interface and interactive visualization to make sure that all functions work correctly.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
